      <TR><TD ALIGN="LEFT"><B>HOW TO READ THE CURRENT WORKFLOW</B></TD></TR>
      <TR><TD ALIGN="LEFT">Column order is source responsibility, not a sequence of imports or runtime calls.</TD></TR>
      <TR><TD ALIGN="LEFT"><B>Assembly:</B> potential -&gt; dynamics; dynamics + initial_conditions -&gt; InitialValueProblem; caller selects method + request.</TD></TR>
      <TR><TD ALIGN="LEFT"><B>Execution:</B> (1) simulate -&gt; (2) new_run -&gt; (3) initialize -&gt; (4) integrate_method -&gt; (5) controller -&gt; (6) advance.</TD></TR>
      <TR><TD ALIGN="LEFT"><B>Completion:</B> repeat (5)-(6), collect and sample; (7) export IntegrationData -&gt; (8) simulate resumes -&gt; (9) Solution.</TD></TR>
      <TR><TD ALIGN="LEFT">Solid arrows: selected calls or required data. Dotted blue: returns. Dashed purple: optional events or analysis. Red dashed: failures.</TD></TR>
      <TR><TD ALIGN="LEFT">Unconnected cards document capabilities or ownership; they do not imply additional runtime stages.</TD></TR>
      <TR><TD ALIGN="LEFT">contracts/ owns shared records; dynamics/protocols.py owns physical capabilities; formulations/base.py owns split-map protocols.</TD></TR>
      <TR><TD ALIGN="LEFT">studies/ assembles experiments; diagnostics/ owns opt-in observers and persistence; visualization/ owns presentation.</TD></TR>
    </TABLE>
  >];
